## Why This Is Asked

This angle tests cross-account SAP design with per-BU isolation, JIT operator access, and PrivateLink auditing.

## Key Concepts

- Cross-account IAM roles and SCPs
- AWS SSO with Just-In-Time elevation
- PrivateLink for SAP components
- Centralized auditing with CloudTrail/Config
- IaC patterns (CDK/CloudFormation)

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal AWS CDK snippet creating cross-account trust role and a VPC endpoint service
import * as iam from 'aws-cdk-lib/aws-iam';
import * as ec2 from 'aws-cdk-lib/aws-ec2';
import { Stack, Construct } from 'aws-cdk-lib';
export class SapCrossAccountStack extends Stack {
  constructor(scope: Construct, id: string) {
    super(scope, id);
    const crossAccountRole = new iam.Role(this, 'SapCrossAccountRole', {
      assumedBy: new iam.AccountPrincipal('111122223333'),
      description: 'Cross-account trust role for SAP BU access',
      roleName: 'SapCrossAccountRole',
    });
    crossAccountRole.addToPolicy(new iam.PolicyStatement({
      actions: ['s3:ListBucket','s3:GetObject'],
      resources: ['arn:aws:s3:::sap-artifacts-*','arn:aws:s3:::sap-artifacts-*/*']
    }));
    new ec2.CfnVPCEndpointService(this, 'SapVpceService', {
      serviceName: 'com.amazonaws.vpce.sap',
      acceptanceRequired: false
    });
  }
}
```

